       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and the usual OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common analgesic or anti-inflammatory dose\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common dose for inflammatory conditions\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you intend and I'll enter it. Please also confirm it with your supervising resident or attending and the pharmacist, since you're a student. If you really do want 4000 mg per dose, I'd need that confirmed by the prescribing physician first."
